     <item>
      <widget class="QLabel" name="about_inputs_label">
       <property name="text">
        <string>&lt;b&gt;EEG spectral power reports&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Add the EEG spectral power reports written by "Analyze EEG Spectral Power". You can add more than one report.&lt;br/&gt;• Each recording of the reports is a subject of "Subjects".&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Channel labels&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Double-click a channel label to edit it.&lt;br/&gt;• Edit it at the subject level, in "Channels of the subject", or at the cohort level, in "Channels of the cohort". A label edited at the cohort level changes for all the subjects loaded.&lt;br/&gt;• Uncheck a channel to remove it.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Regions of interest&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Add a region of interest (ROI) at the cohort level to average several channels together.&lt;br/&gt;• Click "Add ROI", then check the channels to include in the ROI. The list holds the channels of the cohort loaded.&lt;br/&gt;• Check "blank" to leave the ROI empty when data are missing for the mean. Otherwise the missing data are ignored.&lt;br/&gt;• The ROI is named ROI_ followed by its channel labels, with _b at the end when "blank" is checked. For example, ROI_C3C4 for the channels C3 and C4.&lt;br/&gt;• Rename your channel labels first. Adding the ROIs must be the final step.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="textFormat">
        <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
       </property>
       <property name="wordWrap">
        <bool>true</bool>
       </property>
       <property name="variant" stdset="0">
        <string notr="true">help</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
